The '''Avernic defender''' is a [[defender]] wielded in the [[Worn Equipment#Shield slot|shield slot]], requiring 70 [[Attack]] and [[Defence]] to wield. It is obtained by combining a [[dragon defender]] with an [[Avernic defender hilt]]. This process can be reversed to return the dragon defender, but the hilt will be '''destroyed''' in the process. This defender boasts the highest [[Strength#Strength bonus|strength bonus]] of any shield slot equipment, being 1 higher than the [[dragonfire shield]]. It also has the highest [[melee]] [[Attack#Attack bonus|attack bonuses]] of any shield slot equipment. The defensive bonuses are comparable to that of an [[adamant kiteshield]].

[[Ghommal's hilt 5]] or [[Ghommal's hilt 6|6]] can be attached to it, creating [[Ghommal's avernic defender 5]] or [[Ghommal's avernic defender 6|6]] respectively, giving the bonuses of the Avernic defender and the additional benefits of the hilt. This process is reversible, returning both the hilt and the defender.

Avernic weaponry was common amongst [[Zarosian]] forces in the [[Second Age]], crafted by Avernic [[Demons|demon]] smiths in the liquid fires of [[Infernus]]. Today, they are incredibly rare, and [[Verzik Vitur]]'s Avernic defender is one of the few to remain, a relic from her time in the service of [[Zaros]]. Due to its age, the full defender has been destroyed, and only the hilt remains.{{CiteNews|url=http://services.runescape.com/m=news/the-theatre-of-blood?oldschool=1|title=The Theatre of Blood|newsdate=7 June 2018|quote=During the Second Age, Avernic weaponry was common amongst the forces of the Empty Lord. These weapons, crafted by Avernic smiths in the liquid fires of Infernus, were some of the most powerful around. Today, Avernic weapons are incredibly rare, the secrets behind their creation having long since been lost. Lady Verzik's Avernic Defender is one of the few to still remain and is a relic from her time in the service of the Empty Lord. [...] Due to its age, the full defender has been destroyed, leaving behind only the hilt.}}

If the player dies to a [[PvP]] death and the avernic defender is not one of the player's protected items, it will remain in the player's inventory, but will become [[(broken)|broken]], which means the item is unusable and must be repaired with {{NoCoins|600000|c}} by using the item on [[Perdu]]. The game values the defender at 600,000 GP when determining which items to protect.

